From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy Schmidt <timschmidt@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 01:03:36 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_smbb: refresh both battery temperature
 flags

Replace the cached OK and HOT flags together after each successful status read. Without clearing HOT, a later cold indication after a hot interrupt is reported as Overheat. Leave the cached state alone when the register read fails.
---
 drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbb.c | 10 ++++------
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbb.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbb.c
index d054c3865..7eeaada33 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbb.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbb.c
@@ -472,13 +472,11 @@ static irqreturn_t smbb_bat_temp_handler(int irq, void *_data)
 		return IRQ_HANDLED;
 
 	mutex_lock(&chg->statlock);
-	if (val & TEMP_STATUS_OK) {
+	chg->status &= ~(STATUS_BAT_OK | STATUS_BAT_HOT);
+	if (val & TEMP_STATUS_OK)
 		chg->status |= STATUS_BAT_OK;
-	} else {
-		chg->status &= ~STATUS_BAT_OK;
-		if (val & TEMP_STATUS_HOT)
-			chg->status |= STATUS_BAT_HOT;
-	}
+	else if (val & TEMP_STATUS_HOT)
+		chg->status |= STATUS_BAT_HOT;
 	mutex_unlock(&chg->statlock);
 
 	power_supply_changed(chg->bat_psy);
